From: grigio <https://github.com/grigio>
Subject: [PATCH] build-aux: make Cargo builds reproducible

Cargo already ships the release lockfile, so make the Meson build fail
instead of silently changing dependency versions when it is inconsistent.
The package fetches dependencies during prepare(), so the build can also
run fully offline. Keep compiler paths stable and use grep's end-of-options
marker while detecting the release profile.

--- a/build-aux/cargo.sh
+++ b/build-aux/cargo.sh
@@ -3,0 +4,5 @@
+
+# Keep compiler diagnostics and panic metadata free of machine-specific paths.
+SOURCE_DIR="$(cd "$2" && pwd)"
+CARGO_DIR="$(cd "$CARGO_HOME" 2>/dev/null && pwd || printf '%s' "$CARGO_HOME")"
+export RUSTFLAGS="${RUSTFLAGS:-} --remap-path-prefix=$SOURCE_DIR=/build/carosello --remap-path-prefix=$CARGO_DIR=/build/cargo"
@@ -18 +23 @@
-cargo build "${@:4}" || exit 1
+cargo build --frozen --locked "${@:4}" || exit 1
@@ -22 +27 @@
-  if echo "$@" | grep -q "\-\-release"; then
+  if echo "$@" | grep -q -- "--release"; then
@@ -28 +33 @@
-  if echo "$@" | grep -q "\-\-release"; then
+  if echo "$@" | grep -q -- "--release"; then
